# @see R-030 (Design Patterns vs Native Platform Features)
id: PATTERN-004
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 3
action: advisory
title: Missing structured error handling
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .js .tsx .jsx .py .go .rs .java .kt
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: catch\s*\(\s*\w*\s*\)\s*\{\s*\}
    message: "Empty catch block — errors are silently swallowed. Handle, rethrow, or log the error"
  - regex: catch\s*\(\s*\w*\s*\)\s*\{\s*//
    message: "Catch block with only a comment — the error is still swallowed. Add proper error handling"
  - regex: \.catch\(\s*\(\)\s*=>\s*\{\s*\}\s*\)
    message: "Empty .catch() — promise errors are silently ignored. Handle or propagate the error"
  - regex: except:\s*$|except\s+Exception\s*:
    message: "Bare except or catch-all Exception — catch specific errors and handle them appropriately"
  - regex: catch\s*\(Exception\s+
    message: "Catching generic Exception — catch specific exception types for targeted error handling"
fix: Use structured error handling — Result/Either types (Rust, fp-ts), typed exceptions, or at minimum log and rethrow with context. Never silently swallow errors.
